<title>UK: MORGAN GRENFELL LATAM RAISES BRAZIL EXPOSURE.</title>
<headline>MORGAN GRENFELL LATAM RAISES BRAZIL EXPOSURE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Grenfell Latin American Companies Trust said on Wednesday it had increased its exposure to Brazil in July, buying around one million stg of electricity utility Copel.</p>
<p>The fund said it believed the outlook for Brazil remained bright, despite recent currency jitters.</p>
<p>&quot;We are less concerned about the currency outlook than some,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>&quot;Although the trade balance has deteriorated we are estimating a negative $12 billion for the year against which foreign direct investment is likely to total $15 billion and foreign reserves are approximately $60 billion.&quot;</p>
<p>But it remains cautious and underweight on Argentina, despite increasing estimates for GDP, predicting corporate profits growth below that of Brazil and Mexico.</p>
